9	/* Order state for the deploy wizard.
10	 *
11	 * Ported from the design sandbox with ONE structural change, and it is the
12	 * important one: the sandbox derived every money figure here in the browser
13	 * (`dueToday`, `saved`, `walletApplied`, `cardDue`) from a fixture price table.
14	 * None of that survives. The server is asked what the selection costs, and this
15	 * context only holds the answer. A price the browser works out is a second
16	 * pricing formula, and the first time it disagrees with `orderQuote` a customer
17	 * is shown one number and charged another.
18	 *
19	 * Kept exactly as designed:
20	 *  - Choosing a service seeds a COMPLETE, working configuration, so the order is
21	 *    buyable without touching anything. Only free defaults are pre-set; nothing
22	 *    that adds to the total is ever ticked for you.
23	 *  - Once a service is picked nothing is gated — you can commit from anywhere.
24	 *  - This is deliberately NOT a <form>. On the live platform an unkeyed ternary
25	 *    once made Continue and Deploy the same DOM node and charged five customers
26	 *    four steps early. The commit action is its own button and nothing else can
27	 *    submit.
28	 */
